---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Tee Shop">
	<div class="simple-page align-left">
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p><em>Last updated: [date]. This is a starting draft, not legal advice — have it reviewed before relying on it, and update it to match your actual jurisdiction's requirements (e.g. GDPR, CCPA) if applicable.</em></p>

		<h2>1. What we collect</h2>
		<p>
			When you place an order, we collect your email address, shipping address, and order
			details (items, sizes, quantities). We never collect or store your full card number —
			payment is handled entirely by Stripe.
		</p>

		<h2>2. Your cart</h2>
		<p>
			Items you add to your cart are stored only in your browser's local storage, on your own
			device. We don't see your cart contents until you check out.
		</p>

		<h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
		<p>
			We use order information to process payment, fulfill and ship your order, and contact you
			about that order if needed. We don't sell your information.
		</p>

		<h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Stripe</strong> — processes payment and collects your shipping address at checkout.</li>
			<li><strong>Printful</strong> (or our print-on-demand provider) — receives your shipping address and order details to print and ship your item.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Each of these providers has its own privacy policy governing how they handle your data.</p>

		<h2>5. Data retention</h2>
		<p>
			We keep order records for as long as needed for accounting, support, and legal
			requirements.
		</p>

		<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask us what information we hold about you, or ask us to delete it (subject to
			legal recordkeeping requirements), by emailing
			<a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>7. Contact</h2>
		<p>Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a>.</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
